{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-4985-r4494445","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Pork Stomach Filled with Meat and Vegetables (Saumagen)","sourcePageId":4985,"sourceRevision":"4494445","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-05-25T22:48:05Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Pork%20Stomach%20Filled%20with%20Meat%20and%20Vegetables%20(Saumagen)&oldid=4494445","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:20:28.261Z","sourceCategories":["Category:German recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using carrot","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using marjoram","Category:Recipes using meat","Category:Recipes using nutmeg","Category:Recipes using onion","Category:Recipes using pepper","Category:Recipes using pork","Category:Recipes using potato","Category:Recipes using salt","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"a19ab1ab1e2e91943595d8743a10ea2f6bdbe16b71b5a3a0b1773b886ac177a3","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Pork recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* 1 small [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] stomach (order from your butcher)\n* 375 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] fatless [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] belly (''Schweinebauch'')\n* 375 g pork meat\n* 375 g ground meat (''Bratwurstfüllsel'')\n* 1–2 rolls, soaked in some [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Kilogram|kg]] boiled [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrots]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]]\n* 1 bunch of [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]]\n* 1–2 cloves of [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]]\n* [[Cookbook:Marjoram|Marjoram]]\n* [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|Nutmeg]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Soak the pork stomach overnight and use twine to close two of the three apertures. \n#Cut the meat and potatoes into small cubes. \n#Stew the onions, carrots, and parsley in butter. Smash the garlic.\n#Mix everything with the rolls and eggs and spice it well; then put everything into the pork stomach and close the third aperture. \n#Put the stomach in hot water and cook for 2–3 hours. The water must not boil.\n#Cut the stomach in 2 cm thick slices and serve them with mashed potatoes and sauerkraut. Alternatively you can store the cooked stomach in the fridge and fry it when you are ready to eat it.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using pork]]\n[[Category:Recipes using meat]]\n[[Category:German recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using potato]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using nutmeg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using marjoram]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Pork Stomach Filled with Meat and Vegetables (Saumagen)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 small pork stomach (order from your butcher)","sourceText":"1 small pork stomach (order from your butcher)","amountText":"1 small p